<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sitting Bull</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1831–<a href="/years/1890">1890</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Tatanka Iyotake</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sitting Bull was a Hunkpapa Lakota holy man and leader who united Lakota and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheyenne">Cheyenne</a> bands against American expansion onto the Great Plains. His followers defeated Custer at the Little Bighorn in 1876. After years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> he surrendered in 1881, and he was killed by Indian police during an attempt to arrest him in 1890.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sitting-bull.jpg" alt="Sitting Bull" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David F. Barry, Photographer, Bismarck, Dakota Territory · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sitting_Bull_by_D_F_Barry_ca_1883_Dakota_Territory.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
